Make the Mooncake engine-id lookup lazy, so prefill/decode disaggregation works
under Kubernetes service discovery.

THE DEFECT: mooncake_prefill_info -- the table mapping (bootstrap_port, prefill
base URL) to its Mooncake bootstrap address and per-dp-rank engine ids -- is
populated in VllmPDRouter::new only when iterating the static --prefill URL
list in direct-URL mode (src/routers/http/vllm_pd_router.rs). Under Kubernetes
service discovery that construction path receives an empty static list because
workers arrive later through the watcher in src/service_discovery.rs, whose
add_prefill_server calls do not populate the table. Every per-request lookup in
build_decode_kv_transfer_params then misses, logs "No Mooncake bootstrap info,
decode will proceed without kv_transfer_params", and sends decode requests
without remote_engine_id, remote_bootstrap_addr or transfer_id. Even in static
mode, querying only once at construction means a prefiller that restarts under
a new engine id is never re-read.

THE FIX: adapt mooncake_prefill_info onto upstream PR #526 (commit 19b5d8d) as
std::sync::RwLock<MooncakePrefillTable> keyed by (bootstrap_port, base_url),
matching nixl_prefill_info and never holding the lock across .await. On a cache
miss, resolve_mooncake_info resolves the prefiller's bootstrap address via
mooncake_prefill_target (reading bootstrap_port from the worker and falling back
to 8998), queries the bootstrap server with a 3-attempt request budget while
construction keeps 30 attempts, and caches successful results in the RwLock
table. Failures are not cached so subsequent requests retry, and
add_prefill_server, remove_prefill_server, and WorkerManagement::remove_worker
evict cached entries for that URL so restarted prefillers are re-queried.

AGAINST: vllm-project/router commit c132dbc0cfdf5c642c3dca6caa71218f3c3035cb
(post-v0.1.17 main, including PR #520 51c675a and PR #526 19b5d8d), named by
VLLM_ROUTER_COMMIT in pack/llm-router/Dockerfile.

WHEN TO REMOVE: stays until upstream ships runtime Mooncake registration (#209)
or lazy Mooncake bootstrap lookup on the Kubernetes discovery path.

